# Stray (PPSA02101) -- past the brightness-calibration screen to the first map load.
#
# Anchors are SECONDS from the first pad poll (src/input/pad.cpp:207-210 -- a bare number is
# seconds, 'f' is flips, 'p' is pad reads).
#
# VALIDATED on Linux with hardware Vulkan (RADV, AMD Radeon 8060S / STRIX_HALO) at 3840x2160,
# headless `tools/screenshot` frontend, PROSPER_RENDER=1, PROSPER_GUEST_ARGS=-force-gfx-direct,
# no render acceleration. Measured 2026-08-22 on master bb57d617.
#
# THIS IS THE ONE OF THE THREE THAT REALLY IS CROSS-ONLY.
#
# The first-boot screen is the brightness calibration -- three cat silhouettes, a 16-step slider,
# and a prompt bar reading `/\ Defaults` and `X Accept`. Its own prompt names the button and the
# button is correct: CROSS accepts, and nothing else is needed through the main menu behind it.
# Recorded explicitly because the other two routes in this batch are NOT cross-only, and the
# difference is not guessable from the prompt bar -- BALAN's names CROSS on a screen CROSS cannot
# leave, and Unbound's title screen names CROSS while the screen after it names SQUARE.
#
# Positive control that the route drives the guest: with this route the `X Accept` glyph renders
# in its pressed state, and the run leaves a screen a default run never leaves.
#
# PROGRESS ORACLE IS THE FILE LOG, NOT PIXELS (PROSPER_FILELOG=1) -- this title loses most of its
# presents to the #2932 wrong composite. With its negative control:
#
#   default route, no input, 150 s  -> last asset is  /app0/hk_project/config/tags
#                                      NO hk_project_mainstart, on 0 of the run's log lines
#   this route, 415 s               -> /app0/hk_project_mainstart   t~36.5
#
# WHAT THIS ROUTE DOES NOT DO: it does not produce a rendered world. After the map load the frames
# are LETTERBOXED -- black bars top and bottom, i.e. the game's own cinematic framing -- with the
# picture between them a flat single-colour fill. The guest stays alive and keeps flipping. That
# is #2932, not this route, which is why the title is still rung 2. Phase 3 is written for the
# world that map load implies; it has not yet had one to move through.

